    "q-154925": {
      "dom_id": "step-q154925",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $3a-7>\\frac{8a+5}{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-7 & >\\frac{8a+5}{4} \\\\ 4\\cdot (3a-7) & >4\\cdot (\\frac{8a+5}{4}) \\\\ 4\\cdot (3a-7) & >\\cancel{4}\\cdot (\\frac{8a+5}{\\cancel{4}}) \\\\ 4\\cdot (3a-7) & >8a+5 \\\\ 12a-28 & >8a+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12a-28 & >8a+5 \\\\ 12a-28-8a & >8a+5-8a \\\\ 4a-28 & >5 \\\\ 4a-28+28 & >5+28 \\\\ 4a & >33 \\\\ \\frac{4a}{4} & >\\frac{33}{4} \\\\ a & >\\frac{33}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a>\\frac{33}{4}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-154925-a",
