    "q-181376": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181376",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{3-5z}{8}\\le 6-2z.$\n\nThe solution is $z$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3-5z}{8} & \\le 6-2z \\\\ 8\\cdot (\\frac{3-5z}{8}) & \\le 8\\cdot (6-2z) \\\\ \\cancel{8}\\cdot (\\frac{3-5z}{\\cancel{8}}) & \\le 8\\cdot (6-2z) \\\\ 3-5z & \\le 48-16z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-5z & \\le 48-16z \\\\ 3-5z+16z & \\le 48-16z+16z \\\\ 3+11z & \\le 48 \\\\ 3+11z-3 & \\le 48-3 \\\\ 11z & \\le 45 \\\\ \\frac{11z}{11} & \\le \\frac{45}{11} \\\\ z & \\le \\frac{45}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z\\le \\frac{45}{11}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
